{"id":"CVE-2013-4238","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2013-08-18T01:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T16:38:01.666Z","description":"The ssl.match_hostname function in the SSL module in Python 2.6 through 3.4 does not properly handle a '\\0' character in a domain name in the Subject Alternative Name field of an X.509 certificate, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof arbitrary SSL servers via a crafted certificate issued by a legitimate Certification Authority, a related issue to CVE-2009-2408.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2013-1582.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2013:1582"},{"url":"http://www.vmware.com/security/advisories/VMSA-2014-0012.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2013-09/msg00043.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2013:1463"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2013-09/msg00029.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2013:1440"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/534161/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20141205 NEW: VMSA-2014-0012 - VMware vSphere product updates address security vulnerabilities"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2014/dsa-2880","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-2880"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-1982-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-1982-1"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2013-09/msg00026.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2013:1437"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2014/Dec/23","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20141205 NEW: VMSA-2014-0012 - VMware vSphere product updates address security vulnerabilities